      "question": "What diagnostic tests are indicated for this patient?",
      "my_answer": "No urgent diagnostic tests are indicated; a comprehensive eye examination with tear film assessment (e.g., tear break-up time, Schirmer's test) may be performed by an ophthalmologist to confirm dry eye.",
      "rationale": "Given the typical history and normal exam, extensive testing is not needed, but targeted dry eye tests can help quantify the condition and guide management."
    },
    {
      "id": "Q7",
      "question": "What immediate management should be recommended?",
      "my_answer": "Recommend frequent breaks using the 20-20-20 rule, artificial tears for dryness, and optimization of screen ergonomics (e.g., proper distance, lighting, and blink awareness).",
      "rationale": "These measures directly address the underlying causes of eye strain and dryness and are the first-line treatment for computer vision syndrome."
    },
    {
      "id": "Q8",
      "question": "What is the expected prognosis and need for follow-up?",
      "my_answer": "Prognosis is excellent with lifestyle modifications; symptoms should improve. Follow-up is only needed if symptoms persist or worsen despite conservative measures.",
