      "rationale": "The combination of severe sore throat worsening despite antibiotics, trismus, muffled 'hot potato' voice, drooling, bulging soft palate with medial/inferior displacement of the tonsil, and uvula deviation to the contralateral side is classic for a peritonsillar abscess."
